abstract: >-
  OMDA is an open specification for turning paper and digital documents into
  verified, cited records on a phone, readable by any model and any agent. It
  defines model slots, provenance, evidenced assertions, deterministic
  verification, an on-device store, an agent interface bound to MCP, Android
  AppFunctions and iOS App Intents, a skills manifest, and selective-disclosure
  exchange over W3C Verifiable Credentials 2.0 with SD-JWT.
